hi this is Dan Adelman the half of  Thomas have games that isn't actually  Thomas hat I'll be sharing some tips and  tricks for new players of axiom verge to  do that I'm actually going to go into  speed run mode the benefit of speed run  mode is that it removes all of the  cutscenes and story based elements and  lets us jump right into the gameplay but  when you play the game for the first  time you should definitely just start up  a new game in regular mode to get the  full experience if you're new to the  genre you'll notice that the environment  will actually teach you how to play  without bogging you down with tutorials  for example you'll notice that the path  to the right is blocked which lets you  know you sometimes need to go left this  by the way is no Majda metroid which  starts off the same way definitely keep  an eye out for these environmental cues  here you'll notice that there's no way  out unless you shoot through these red  blobs which teaches you how to shoot and  navigate your way through the  environment  one thing I noticed when watching new  players is that they die quickly when  they just try to run through the  environment almost every enemy you  encounter can actually either be avoided  completely or destroyed from a position  where you can hit them but they can't  hit you I recommend taking your time as  you go through the different rooms and  see if you can find a plan of attack  that will keep you safe for example  there's no way for me to avoid this  enemy completely if I just run up to it  the bugs that keep spawning from it will  damage me but if I jump up onto this  platform I can attack it safely  sometimes the best spot to attack from  will require you to shoot at an angle to  do that hold down the L button to lock  your position and keep yourself from  moving around while you shoot we're  about to meet the first boss I won't  show you the entire fight but i'll show  you how to approach it you'll notice  that this boss has two different attacks  first are these projectiles that do  damage on impact you'll need to keep  shooting while avoiding these I like  standing on these blocks locking my  position and just shooting it the boss  until I need to move out of the way the  second attack is similar to the first  but it only does damage after it  explodes which is a second or two after  it hits the ground just make sure where  you're stepping so you're not in the  blast radius when it goes off  exploration is a big theme in axiom  verge if you ever find that you're not  sure where to go next be sure to check  your map on the gamepad there's probably  some door you haven't gone through yet  or room that you haven't finished  exploring here we find probably the most  distinctive upgrading the game the  address disruptor the address disruptor  lets you glitch the environment and  enemies to uncover hidden secrets  throughout the world as in the beginning  of the game there's no way to progress  here until you demonstrate your ability  to use the address disruptor by  glitching these platforms into existence  every creature an axiom verge can be  glitched some enemies in there glitched  form become helpful in some way some  become more aggressive and some just do  bizarre things as i mentioned  exploration is a primary theme of the  game so i definitely encourage you to  try glitching every enemy type at least  once for example you may remember this  enemy type from the beginning of the  game if I glitch it instead of spawning  bugs to attack me it now spawns health  glitching these round pink guys makes  them able to break through walls which  will allow you to get access to a hidden  powerup  and notice how if I glitch this guy all  of the enemies of the same type also get  glitched and if I destroy one I destroy  them all these are just some of the ways  that exploration and experimentation  will aid you on your mission this has  been Dan Adelman from Thomas app games  and I hope you enjoyed these tips and  tricks for axiom verge
 

